            <ArticleTitle>Endobronchial lipoma: a rare cause of bronchial occlusion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>494-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.arbres.2013.03.009</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0300-2896(13)00097-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Endobronchial lipoma is a rare benign neoplasm of the tracheobronchial tree. Despite its benign nature, associated endoluminal polypoid growth can cause bronchial occlusion. In this paper, we present the consequences of a late diagnosis of this condition.</AbstractText>
